/target
crates/zipp-wasm/target/
crates/zipp-sandbox/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock is committed — Zipp ships the `zipp` CLI, so a
# locked dependency set keeps builds reproducible.


# Generated wasm-bindgen glue for the node harnesses (see crates/zipp-wasm/tests/node/README.md)
crates/zipp-wasm/tests/node/pkg/
# ...and for the browser target, which the README recipe and SoftN's vendoring
# script both write here. Untracked build output blocks the clean-checkout rule
# that vendoring depends on, exactly as dist/ did.
crates/zipp-wasm/pkg/

# Release packaging output. The release job writes the CLI archive to ./dist and
# the browser bundle to crates/zipp-wasm/dist, so anyone reproducing those steps
# locally ends up with an untracked tree. That is not cosmetic: SoftN's vendoring
# script refuses to stamp a WASM binary with a revision when `git status` is not
# clean, so build output left here blocks the documented way to pick up an engine.
dist/

# Python bytecode cache from tools/ (bench.py is imported by test_bench.py)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Agent worktrees and session state
.claude/

# A/B comparison binaries. Routine JSON also belongs under ignored target/;
# bench/ retains only deliberately reviewed canonical or historical evidence.
# Executables are rebuildable from the commit recorded by the retained artifact.
bench/bin/
zipp_profiling.map
target-hard1/
target-hard2/
target-soft/

# Browser package built by `wasm-bindgen --target web` (see crates/zipp-wasm/README.md).
crates/zipp-wasm/pkg/
